+# LOSSY-VERIFICATION PILOT PATCH (not upstream vLLM).
+#
+# Speculative Cascades [OPT] (spec-casc-opt), Narasimhan et al. 2025, "Faster
+# Cascades via Speculative Decoding". A training-free relaxed target
+# distribution that -- per position -- either defers to the strict p/q test
+# or skips it and accepts the draft token outright:
+#
+#   defer  iff  max_u q(u) < max_u p(u) - alpha * TV(p, q)
+#   accept iff  defer and p(x)/q(x) >= u,  OR  not defer (always)
+#
+# alpha is a real number (not restricted to (0, 1] like the lenience factor):
+# more negative alpha defers more often (alpha -> -inf recovers strict
+# spec-dec exactly, since max_u p(u) - alpha*TV -> +inf makes "max_u q(u) <
+# ..." always true); alpha=0 is the paper's own suggested minimum but the
+# reproduction paper (arXiv:2607.08690) found it too high for an MTP drafter
+# in practice, defaulting to +inf when unreadable is the fail-safe direction
+# so a missing config file degrades to strict rather than to "always trust q".
+#
+# Distinct from lenience: lenience boosts accept probability for the ACTUAL
+# drafted token x only (a 1D per-token ratio test); spec-casc-opt's decision
+# needs max_u q(u), max_u p(u) and TV(p,q) -- reductions over the FULL vocab
+# distributions -- computed once in plain PyTorch in rejection_sample() below
+# (mirroring relaxation_trace.py's already-validated target_top1_prob/tv_distance
+# computation) and passed into the kernel as a per-token boolean mask, rather
+# than reimplemented as a new full-vocab Triton reduction.
+#
+# Mutually exclusive with the lenience patch: both touch the same pristine
+# file, so only one can be applied to a given vLLM install at a time. See
+# patches/apply_spec_casc_opt.sh.
+#
+# The alpha value comes from a file, not the environment: vLLM spawns
+# EngineCore with a sanitised environment, so env vars never reach the
+# sampler (see the lenience patch's identical note; that failure produced two
+# bogus datasets before it was caught for a simpler one-parameter patch, so
+# this one is loud about it too). The path is uid-scoped under /tmp so a
+# clone in any directory agrees with the server script.
+_SPEC_CASC_FORCE_COMMIT_ALPHA_FILE = f"/tmp/lossy-token-eff-spec-casc-opt-force-commit-alpha-{os.getuid()}"
